Article 13
Every person who knows, sees, or hears the occurrence of domestic violence is obligated to make efforts according to their capacity to:
a. prevent the continuation of the criminal act;
b. provide protection to the victim;
c. provide emergency assistance; and/or
d. assist in the process of submitting a request for a protection order.

Article 17
(1) Forms of services for victims include:
a. consultation, complaint, and accompaniment services;
b. health services;
c. social rehabilitation services;
d. legal services; and
e. social reintegration services.
(2) In addition to being carried out by the Government, services can be carried out by:
a. community;
b. family; and
c. volunteers.
(3) Implementation of services must be based on:
a. quick response;
b. empathy;
c. non-discrimination;
d. confidentiality;
e. accessibility;
f. professionalism; and
g. free of charge.
(4) Health services as referred to in paragraph (1) letter b include:
a. counseling;
b. medical examination;
c. treatment;
d. medical rehabilitation;
e. issuance of medical evidence; and
f. referral to health services.
(5) Health services as referred to in paragraph (4) are carried out by medical personnel and paramedics; and
c. referral to health services.

