CHAPTER VI
COMMUNITY PARTICIPATION
Article 38
(1) The community participates and plays a role in the implementation of protection for Victims.
(2) Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be in the form of:
a. establishing partner families at the village/kelurahan level;
b. establishing women and children protection units in community organizations;
c. conducting independent socialization of women's and children's rights;
d. providing first aid to victims; and So that everyone may know of it, orders with REGIONAL PROTECTION REGULATION

